PolishPolitics.cabinet1922View(Q);
!}

= The cabinet of Ponikowski resigns

After a dispute with the Naczelnik Państwa over the cabinet, Antoni Ponikowski hands in his resignation and stays as caretaker until a new cabinet is appointed. In this game the Naczelnik prefers his own candidate, Artur Śliwiński; any cabinet still needs the support of the Sejm. The course of the dispute is a scenario profile of the game, based on the chronology of the cabinets of 1922.

PPS chooses how it enters the formation. The formation card then shows every setting of our offer before it is submitted.

- @pils_candidate
- @parliamentary_compromise
- @opposition

@pils_candidate
title: Support the Naczelnik's candidate, Artur Śliwiński
subtitle: The formation starts with him as prime minister of a non-party cabinet that PPS supports from outside. If the Sejm does not carry him, the next feasible offer is weighed.
choose-if: {! return PolishPolitics.cabinet1922Status(Q, 'pils_candidate').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_b1_pils_candidate_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishPolitics.cabinet1922Choose(Q, 'pils_candidate');
!}
go-to: polish_cabinet_formation

@parliamentary_compromise
title: Seek a compromise candidate of the Sejm
subtitle: The formation starts with Julian Nowak as prime minister of a non-party cabinet that PPS supports from outside.
choose-if: {! return PolishPolitics.cabinet1922Status(Q, 'parliamentary_compromise').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_b1_parliamentary_compromise_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishPolitics.cabinet1922Choose(Q, 'parliamentary_compromise');
!}
go-to: polish_cabinet_formation

@opposition
title: Stay in opposition
subtitle: PPS leaves the formation to the other parties; they form a cabinet if they can.
choose-if: {! return PolishPolitics.cabinet1922Status(Q, 'opposition').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_b1_opposition_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishPolitics.cabinet1922Choose(Q, 'opposition');
!}
go-to: polish_cabinet_formation
